sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: rule 1 (read-only from Node agent reports, like tool.adopt), R1 record-only default, R4 Node-work branch; .env stays the user's file; Processes from Project definitions (instance.create). docs/domains/applications.md#register-an-existing-checkout.
  %% Revised: Nick 2026-11-03. Default: check and record, no run. --setup and --domain are opt-in Node work. A linked worktree of the Project's repository is accepted. Caller-agnostic.
  %% Implemented: the record-only default checks the Node agent's checkout fact (agent 0.8.0, 2026-11-03). Not yet: linked worktrees, --setup and --domain are still refused (operation.kind_unavailable); this chart is the target.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: instance:register
  %% kind: instance.register
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane A icon=server pill=observer tone=amber
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>on Node 12
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant A as Node agent<br/>orbit-agent
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  loop continuously, on change
    A->>GW: Report checkouts<br/>with observed_at
    %%> What it observes:
    %%> - each Git checkout under `<apps-root>/<project-slug>/<name>`: owner, layout (checkout or linked worktree), origin, branch, `HEAD` commit, dirty state
    %%> - whether `.env` exists and who can read it; PHP version and the Laravel flag
    %%> Today:
    %%> - the agent reports only task checkouts; until it reports app checkouts, the run reads the checkout over `@swamp/ssh` (interim)
    %%> Runs as:
    %%> - read-only; the Node agent never changes a Node
  end
  CLI->>GW: instance:register<br/>--project=7
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `cd /fast/apps/acme/feature && orbit instance:register --project=7 --yes`; the name defaults to the directory, `feature`
  %%> - syntax: `--project=ID [--path=PATH] [--name=NAME] [--root=PATH] [--setup] [--domain=HOST] [--yes] [--json]`
  %%> What registering means:
  %%> - Orbit adopts a checkout that already exists, in place; a later `instance:destroy` deletes it
  %%> Opt-in:
  %%> - `--setup` runs the Project setup steps and starts its Processes
  %%> - `--domain` creates a Route
  %%> Confirmation:
  %%> - without `--yes`, the CLI asks for consent that names the source; `--json` needs `--yes`
  Note over GW: Check against the facts<br/>path · origin · layout
  %%> Checks:
  %%> - Node 12 has `app-dev`, Project 7 may be placed on it, the name is free
  %%> - the checkout is under `/fast/apps/acme/`, owned by the Node's user, with Project 7's origin
  %%> - a plain checkout, or a linked worktree whose shared `.git` belongs to that repository
  %%> - with `--domain`: the domain is in Node 12's TLD and free (`route.domain_conflict`, 422)
  %%> - the agent's report is fresh enough to trust
  alt facts match
    Note over GW: Record the Instance<br/>Instance 42 · branch feature
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Instance 42 recorded with the observed branch, commit and application facts
    %%> - Git `HEAD`, the index, dirty files and `.env` stay as they are
    opt --setup, --domain or a public .env
      Note over GW: Record intent, start run<br/>task #5131
      %%> When:
      %%> - only when the Node needs work; without it the Instance is active now and no run starts (R1)
      %%> Inputs:
      %%> - Node 12's address and host keys, the facts, the setup steps, the Process definitions, the Route intent
      GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-register
      SW->>N: Protect the .env<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · 0640 orbit-env
      %%> When:
      %%> - only when `.env` exists and others can read it
      %%> How:
      %%> - root runs `chgrp -h orbit-env`, which never follows a link, then the account sets mode 0640; never reads or changes the content
      opt --setup
        SW->>N: Run Project setup steps<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · in order
        %%> What it does:
        %%> - runs the Project's setup steps in the checkout, in order, for example creating `.env`, `composer install`, `php artisan key:generate`
        SW->>N: Create, start Processes<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd · forEach
        %%> What it does:
        %%> - creates and starts the Project's development Processes, as `instance:create` does
      end
      opt --domain
        SW->>N: Create the Route<br/>child route-create
        %%> What it does:
        %%> - the same child workflow as `route:create`: CSR on the Node, the Gateway signs it, install the certificate, publish the Caddy site, probe it over TLS
      end
      alt every step passes
        SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
        Note over GW: Record the result<br/>Instance 42 active · URL
      else a step fails
        SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
        Note over GW: Keep Instance, mark failed<br/>rerun after a fix
        %%> On the Node:
        %%> - the checkout stays as it is; no rollback
      end
    end
    GW-->>CLI: Instance 42<br/>or task #5131 to follow
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - without Node work: the Instance at once (HTTP 201)
    %%> - with Node work: the task (HTTP 202); the CLI follows it with `operation:show` every 2 s
  else mismatch or report too old
    GW--xCLI: Refused or can't verify<br/>instance.source_invalid
    %%> Result:
    %%> - nothing is recorded; fix the source, or try again when the agent reports
  end
